From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sargo@sargo.cc>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 19:27:35 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 47/47] Plutonium: the status cluster: clock, battery and quick
 settings in the title bar

At the title bar's right end, shown whatever else is open: the time, the
battery when not on AC, and an icon for offline or muted. A click opens
quick settings over the helper's desktop services: the date and a
calendar, volume and output, brightness, Wi-Fi and Bluetooth, what's
playing, the battery, and lock, suspend, log out, restart and power off.

Its width is --plutonium-status-width; --workspace-controls-right adds it,
so the panel toggles sit left of it, and the chat header, the panel's tab
strip and the page headers reserve it. Only in the Plutonium shell.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
